-- hit/change-description whole --
Implement pipeline step cancellation on failure

Independent steps kept running after another step failed, leading to wasted resources and late error reports. The linked token is set on the context during the run, allowing cancellation to reach every step. The token is restored in a finally block, ensuring the context is clean. When one step fails, the linked token is triggered, preventing new steps from starting.

